    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0139" n="127" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.203/2–2743</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-27">December 27, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador<anchor n="37" xml:id="d82-f1"/> called at his request and
                    brought up very specially the subject matter of a recent cable from Mr.
                        Winant,<anchor n="38" xml:id="d82-f2"/> in which he set forth the British
                    complaint about the lack of British jurisdiction to punish Americans for crimes
                    committed in that country apart from those pertaining to the duties and
                    functions of seamen. I thanked him and said that this was primarily a matter for
                    the War Department, but that his arguments seemed plausible at first blush to
                    the extent that it might call for further examination or review by my Government
                    and that in any event I would be glad to encourage by suitable means the
                    hastening of consideration of this matter by the War Department coupled with any
                    legitimate cooperation on the part of the State Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d82-f1" n="37" xml:id="d82-f1-content">
                <p>Lord Halifax.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d82-f2" n="38" xml:id="d82-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably reference is to telegram No. 7845, November 11, 1943 (not printed),
                    from John G. Winant, American Ambassador in the United Kingdom.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
